Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:34:50 +0200
Subject: Grow Lyra Ultra userdata partition to 64M

On an 11.5M ext4 filesystem the 4M journal and inode tables leave only
6.8M usable. Move userdata to 0x10000 with 64M and start rootfs after it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .chips/rk3506/parameter-lyra-ultra-emmc.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.chips/rk3506/parameter-lyra-ultra-emmc.txt b/.chips/rk3506/parameter-lyra-ultra-emmc.txt
index 1e16d82..8adf65e 100644
--- a/.chips/rk3506/parameter-lyra-ultra-emmc.txt
+++ b/.chips/rk3506/parameter-lyra-ultra-emmc.txt
@@ -9,5 +9,5 @@ CHECK_MASK: 0x80
 PWR_HLD: 0,0,A,0,1
 TYPE: GPT
 GROW_ALIGN: 0
-CMDLINE: mtdparts=rk29xxnand:0x00002000@0x00002000(uboot),0x00006000@0x00004000(boot),0x00000400@0x0000A000(env),0x00005C00@0x0000A400(userdata),-@0x00010000(rootfs:grow)
+CMDLINE: mtdparts=rk29xxnand:0x00002000@0x00002000(uboot),0x00006000@0x00004000(boot),0x00000400@0x0000A000(env),0x00020000@0x00010000(userdata),-@0x00030000(rootfs:grow)
 uuid:rootfs=614e0000-0000-4b53-8000-1d28000054a9
